Prologue

――The hot air of the fire scorched his lungs, he couldn’t help but violently cough in pain.

???:「――Gh」

He shook his head around, as if he were panting, in search of fresh air.

However, the only air available around him was consumed by the flames. Covering his mouth with his sleeves, he filled his lungs with some semi-adequate air, and moved forward, mustering all of his willpower.

――The city lay beyond recognition.

The once vibrant streets, which had been filled by people going about their daily lives, were now a shadow of their former selves, completely destroyed, the symbol of people’s lives now painted in destruction. 

Scorched roads, trees engulfed in violent flames, collapsed buildings, the wails of the masses echoing throughout.

???:「――」

Gritting his teeth, opening his eyes against the smoke that infiltrated them, he moved forward. —He moved towards the battlefield.  

Indeed, a battlefield. This place was a battlefield.

Once again, he found himself in the familiar hell of a battlefield; a hell utterly submersed in blood, smoke, and death.

And amidst the zeal of his thoughts, what flitted through his mind was the memory of his first battle.

—On that day, he had also been submerged in scorching heat, as his lonesome, bloodied figure strode across the battlefield.

Back then he’d been a wretchedly miserable and weak rookie, unaware of the customs of the battlefield, lacking in the means of survival, merely struggling to stay alive.

Him surviving his first battle came neither from an awakening of some hidden skill, nor the triggering of human instincts of survival, nor the descent of any savior.

He’d just been lucky. He’d just had better luck than the ones who had perished back on that battlefield.

—Then, what about this time? Would it be the same way? Was him surviving down to luck?

???:「—tgh」

—No. Absolutely not.

This time, things were different from then. This battlefield was not one where you could survive depending on your luck.

Furthermore, the tune his heart followed had entirely changed. Back then, he had no reason to fight; it had only come about from conformity, and shallow shows of heroism.

He’d had no reason to fight. Nor a desire to live, only a desire to not die. If his present self hadn’t changed at all, his feet would have directed him far away from all this. If he just wanted to survive, he should have run.

—But, that wasn’t going to happen.

His feet were taking him to the heart of the city; the front line of this battlefield.

???:「——KRUAAAAAAAAAAAGH!!」

A sky, torn asunder by shades of red and of destruction— and a resounding roar, engulfing the city.

Eclipsing the sorrowful howls of the masses, drowning out the sounds of collapse of the falling buildings, and dissatisfied even still, a sound which forced itself upon the world; that was the thundering cry of the Black Dragon.

Hearts quaked at the mighty roar of the Blight Dragon. Footsteps stopped in their tracks, while countless soldiers fell, dropping their swords. Sparing them only a sidelong glance, he pressed onward. Ceaselessly onward. Without pause. Ever onward.

Because, in reach of the Dragon’s awful fangs and claws, stood his comrade in arms.

???:「W̴i̴l̴ḧ̵́e̵̓l̶m̴̌…!」

His old wounds ached. His damaged throat wouldn’t let him clearly utter the name of neither his friend, nor his loved one.

And yet, he still cried out the name of his comrade. He called out to him.

That roused his heart. There, his comrade stood. There, the『Sword Demon』 waited.

The Sword Demon:「GRAAAAAAAA—!!」

The Black Dragon:「KRUUUUUUUAGH—!!」

In that moment, the roars of two shadows, cutting across the scorched crimson sky, collided. 

Clashing head-on with the utterly enormous shadow, its wings unfurled, was an absolutely tiny one of a person. With no wings of its own, it kicked out at its opponent and sprung up into the air, raining countless beams of silver upon his enemy’s massive body. 

However, its massive body swerved away with a flap of its wings, effortlessly grabbing up above its head, countering with its deadly claws.

Continuous were the sounds of blows clashing, the rain of destruction, the impacts which bid tears from the sky above, as dark clouds were torn asunder, giving birth to light.

Overwhelming. Truly overwhelming, was this peak of the sword, forever unparalleled, unreachable by anyone.

This spectacle was such where thinking there was no reaching that battlefield, dismissing it as the realms of transcendents, and resigning oneself to defeat were only natural.

???:「――」

—Even so, he would embark on this journey.

Because the『Sword Demon』, Wilhelm, his comrade, his dear friend, fought there.

A battlefield, scorched with searing flame, a whirlpool of chaos and lament; even in that hell, the fetters of trust and camaraderie remained sound.

???:「…W̶̅a̴͐i̴̽t̷ ̶͉̓f̴o̶͊r̴̒ ̴̛̦m̸̩̔e̶」

I am on my way. Setting out, right this second. Without fail, I shall reach you.

—I won’t let you fight alone. Ever.

Carrying his determination and resolve, the young man, Grimm Fauzen, embarked on a journey through the city stained in red.

Echoing throughout, were the roars of the『Three Headed』Blight Dragon Valgren, like flashes of thunder.

Still indomitable as ever,『The Sword Demon』Wilhelm let out a throat-rending yell.

—The flames of『The Subjugation of the Blight Dragon』burned ever brighter, as if mocking the infinitesimal resistance of mankind.

