Miklotov:「I’d doubted His Majesty Gionis’ thinking, like I always do, back when he entrusted me with you.」

The Giant:「That’s pretty reasonable I reckon. That geezer’s touched in the head. But he convinced me as well. If that blundering fool’s head is like that, then it stands to reason that his limbs are also moving on their own」

Miklotov:「…Be it for better or worse, His Majesty is a fine, upstanding gentleman」

Miklotov pictured his liege’s good-natured smiling face and then slowly shook his head. Then he turned back to face the Giant again.

Miklotov:「But it still surprises me, even now. You should have hated the Kingdom, along with us humans. So why did you help us out?」

